title: Military Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: military_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: marcher_in_government = 1 and army_minister_party = "Marcher" and military_policy_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/LeberJulius.jpg
#subtitle: Dealing with the Commonwealth Army.

= Military Policy

The Commonwealth Army is a deeply <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> institution that has been generally hostile to any notion of <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span> or democracy. However, we now control the military as part of the government. What should we do to reform it?

- @increase_funding: Increase funding for the military to purchase its loyalty.
- @rearmament: Order a significant rearmament of the Commonwealth Army.
- @decrease_funding: Reduce funding for the military so we have more for social spending.
- @reform: Conduct a thorough reform of the ranks, reducing the influence of <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span> and making it more hospitable to us.
- @root: No change to military policy.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@increase_funding
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if coalition_dissent > 0; army_loyalty += 0.07 if army_loyalty < 1; army_strength += 20; left_dissent += 5; collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; west_relation -= 1; east_relation -= 1; reparations_negotiation -= 1; eu_progress -= 1; gold_left += 1; gold_relation += 4; lvp_relation += 4; ddp_relation += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1; ddp_right += 1; lvp_left += 1; goal_marcher_cancel += 1; dufour_angry -= 10; economic_growth += 0.1

The military and the center-right parties are pleasantly surprised that we would increase military funding. Our membership tends to be anti-military, and is less enthused. The Commonwealth's neighbors are watching our military buildup with worry. [? if war_loans >= 0 : This is not good for the War Loans negotiations. ?]

@decrease_funding
subtitle: +1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: army_strength > 0
on-arrival: budget += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition == 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if (in_weimar_coalition and lvp_formed); gold_relation -= 8; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 6; unionist_relation -= 4; army_militancy -= 1; army_strength -= 20; warden_strength += 15; loyalist_strength += 5; warden_militancy += 0.05; army_loyalty -= 0.05 if army_loyalty > 0; coup_progress += 1; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty < 0.2; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty < 0.1; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty <= 0; army_goal_completed = 1; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; lvp_right += 2; army_goal_marcher += 1; dufour_angry += 10; economic_growth -= 0.1

The military has fewer guns and fewer soldiers. There is no hint of a coup yet, but we do not know where the line will be drawn. The center-right parties are committed to the military and deeply opposed to our budget cuts.

Many demobilized soldiers have joined the right-wing paramilitaries such as the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, and weapons are missing from our stockpiles.

@reform
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1 and army_loyalty < 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 1 : We do not have the budget. ?][? if army_loyalty >= 1 : The Commonwealth Army is already fully loyal to the democratic government. ?]
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1 if (in_grand_coalition or (in_weimar_coalition and lvp_formed)); army_loyalty += 0.15; army_militancy -= 0.5 if army_loyalty < 0.5; budget -= 1; coup_progress += 1; gold_relation -= 5; pacifism += 1; democratization += 1; gold_right += 2; ddp_left += 1; lvp_right += 1; dufour_angry += 5;

Our efforts are at least somewhat successful; we have changed the recruiting and training patterns so that more soldiers from non-<span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> backgrounds can join, hopefully changing the culture of the forces. We have also removed some of the officers who supported the previous Avriza putsch.

The center-right parties are committed to the military and deeply suspicious of our efforts to reform it.

@rearmament
subtitle: -2 budget. The most we can do for the forces, and we answer for it ourselves.
choose-if: budget >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget for a programme on this scale.
on-arrival: budget -= 2; army_strength += 55; army_militancy += 0.5 if army_militancy < 8; army_loyalty += 0.1 if army_loyalty < 1; military_confidence += 2; knight_dissent -= 10; knight_strength += 5; left_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 6; labor_dissent += 4; commons_marcher -= 3; dufour_angry -= 12; gold_relation += 5; lvp_relation += 5; unionist_relation += 3; gold_left += 2; lvp_left += 2; imperial_fear -= 1 if imperial_fear > 0; economic_growth += 0.2; west_relation -= 1; east_relation -= 1; reparations_negotiation -= 1; goal_marcher_cancel += 1

Because the ministry is ours, the programme is ours to write: new formations, new equipment, new depots, and a budget line the General Staff had not dared to ask for. It is the largest single expansion the Commonwealth has voted since the Founding, and it is signed by a <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marcher**</span> minister.

The effect on the officer corps is immediate. Men who would not shake our hands a year ago now concede, stiffly, that the party of reform has done more for the forces than the parties of order ever did, and obedience to this government begins to take root. Army loyalty and the officers' confidence in us both rise.

The reaction within our own ranks is another matter. The Left is furious at the sight of Reformists arming the institution that has broken every workers' rising in living memory. The centrists complain about priorities and the social budget. Even the Free Guilds ask what these Crowns might have bought in wages and pensions. Dissent rises across the Left, the centre, and Labor. [? if neorevisionism > 0: The neorevisionists alone among our wings are delighted. ?][? if neorevisionism == 0: One current in the party watches all this with quiet interest. It has been waiting for exactly this argument. ?]

